> Here's a table by numerical luck values I built about
> getting crowned and what other benefits might be
> received:

NetHack uses integer division; you seem to have used normal rounding
to create your table.  Here's a corrected version:

12, 13 - Gives 9 on down. This gives a 2/9 chance of being
crowned, and a 7/9 chance of counting down through the
benefits.

10, 11 - Gives 8 on down. This gives a 1/8 chance of being
crowned, and a 7/8 chance down through the benefits.

8, 9 - Gives 7 on down.  From this point down there is
zero chance of getting crowned.  The results can be:
a) Blessed spellbook, b) AC/protection, c) uncurse all
held items (light blue), d) hit points (golden), e) (golden),
f) fix and bless weapon, or g) nothing in equal chances.
Wonderfull for a spellcaster!

6, 7 - Luck=6 gives 6 on down.  The results can be:
a) AC/protection, b) light blue, c) golden, d) golden,
e) weapon, and f) nothing in equal chances.  Wonderfull
for a combat wombat!

4, 5 - The results can be: a) light blue, b) golden,
c) golden, d) weapon, e) nothing in equal chances.  At
this point we've dropped off being able to gain protection,
but there's still the option of getting a golden glow.  The
golden glow increases max hit points so it remains a
valuable result.

2, 3 - The results can be: a) golden, b) golden,
c) weapon, d) nothing.  Having known positive luck leads
to good results when praying.

0, 1 - The results can be: a) golden, b) weapon, c) nothing.

Keep in mind that the 3) golden glow result only gives a golden glow
the third and subsequent times it is received (before that it gives
the entirely useless castle hint and relatively useless castle
passtune)

Also keep in mind that 5) gives useful intrinsics if you don't have
them before giving AC.

> Also because all troubles are fixed at prayer if your luck
> is positive, wear some of the cursed armor items and

Not necessarily; depends on a roll of d(Luck+location_bonus). If you
have troubles, you may only get some/all of the troubles fixed instead
of getting a favor.  High luck makes getting all+favor likely, but no
troubles and high alignment guarantees a favor.


